:
> > >  Okay, what is the best working parser we have right now?
> >
> > I'm also interested in this. Anybody knows?
>
> Define "best".
>

Most useful, in the same way that a Swiss Army knife is more useful than a
Bowie knife.


> The official parser is, well, most official;
> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=3DOfficial+Parser
>
> camxes is, in many people's eyes, the best encoding of actual Lojban
> as it is used/spoken (the "ku joi" problem, for example, is largely
> considered a wart, not a true part of the language).
> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=3Dcamxes
>

I would agree that camxes. is the current best working parser.


> jbofihe does glossing, but has a number of significant bugs in how
> it handles the language  http://www.rc0.org.uk/jbofihe/


jbofi'e is the only working parser with glossing, which makes it the best
"parser with glossing", but I would not say it is the best by any stretch.


> There are no other parsers I'm aware of.  LogGloss is just a wrapper
> on camxes as far as I know, but it may be using the PEG directly; I
> don't know, I've never looked at or used it.  Someone should ask
> Chris to fix his server, or come find me and we can talk about
> hosting.
>
>
My understanding of LojGloss is that it takes the output of a camxes. parse
and glosses it, with lots of user-friendly bells and whistles. since I
consider the camxes. parsing to be better than the jbofi'e parsing, were
LojGloss to work, I would consider it to be the best.

Is Chris even still around? I don't think he's said anything for awhile now=
.
Have any of you IRC frequenters seen him recently in there?


> -Robin
